{"shortDescription":"Spot basis bids for soybeans were steady to weaker at processors and elevators in the U.S. Midwest on Friday, reflecting moderate farmer sales this week and the approach of the harvest, merchandisers said.Basis values are quoted against CBOT futures in cents/bu:NOTE: 0 = Option Price, UNC = Unchang…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Spot basis bids for soybeans were steady to weaker at processors and elevators in the U.S. Midwest on Friday, reflecting moderate farmer sales this week and the approach of the harvest, merchandisers said."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The spot basis weakened by 10 to 15 cents a bushel at soy processing sites in Decatur, Illinois, and Des Moines, Iowa, spot checks showed, and bigger discounts were scheduled for soybeans delivered in late September and October, when harvest activity should increase."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Hot and dry weather in much of the Midwest was advancing crop maturity. Combines were already rolling in southern areas of Missouri and Illinois, brokers said this week."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Soybean bids also softened at Davenport, Iowa, on the Mississippi River, and Morris, Illinois, on the Illinois River, as rising costs for barge freight depressed grain bids at river elevators."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Corn basis bids were mostly flat, spot checks showed, but the basis fell by a dime at a Chicago processing site and by 7 cents at a Columbus, Ohio, rail terminal."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Farmers increased spot sales of corn and soy this week as futures prices on the Chicago Board of Trade touched multi-year highs. Some grain buyers that had offered large premiums for immediate deliveries of corn and soy were weakening quick-ship bids as more supplies arrived."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type"